/**
 * @defgroup start_stop_compressor_assessment Start/Stop Compressor Model
 * @ingroup compressor_modeling
 * @brief Average power and airflow for a compressor that cycles fully on and fully off.
 * @details
 * Start/stop control assumes the on-cycle package power is represented by the average of the
 * full-load and maximum power fractions. The fraction of time on is represented by the airflow
 * fraction. Use this model only when the compressor actually stops between load periods; unloaded
 * running belongs in a load/unload model.
 *
 * @image html ca-start-stop.svg "Normalized start/stop curve from the 89.5 kW, 560 acfm test fixture."
 *
 * @heading{Performance Curve and Outputs}
 * @formula{start-stop-average-fraction;
 *   f_{avg}=\frac{f_{P,FL}+f_{P,max}}{2}
 * }
 * @formula{start-stop-power-from-airflow;
 *   P=f_{avg}f_QP_{FL}
 * }
 * @formula{start-stop-airflow-from-power;
 *   Q=Q_{FL}\frac{f_P}{f_{avg}}
 * }
 *
 * @heading{Inputs and Origins}
 * Full-load package power and airflow come from measurement or manufacturer data. Maximum and
 * full-load power fractions describe the on-cycle power band and are dimensionless. Select screw or
 * reciprocating construction when applying pressure/inlet correction. The legacy four-input form
 * retains screw behavior; the explicit compressor-type form should be used when construction is known.
 *
 * @symtable
 * @symrow{f_{avg}; Average on-cycle power fraction; \unitless}
 * @symrow{f_{P,FL}; Lower on-cycle power fraction; \unitless}
 * @symrow{f_{P,max}; Maximum on-cycle power fraction; \unitless}
 * @symrow{P; Calculated average package power; \kilo\watt}
 * @symrow{Q; Calculated average delivered airflow; \acfm}
 * @symrow{P_{FL}; Corrected full-load package power; \kilo\watt}
 * @symrow{Q_{FL}; Corrected full-load airflow; \acfm}
 * @symrow{f_P; Average package power fraction; \unitless}
 * @symrow{f_Q; Average airflow fraction or on-time fraction; \unitless}
 * @endsymtable
 *
 * @heading{Fully Substituted Example}
 * For @math{P_{FL}=89.5\ \mathrm{kW}}, @math{Q_{FL}=560\ \mathrm{acfm}},
 * @math{f_{P,FL}=1.00}, @math{f_{P,max}=1.05}, and @math{f_Q=0.20},
 * @math{f_{avg}=(1.00+1.05)/2=1.025}. Therefore
 * @math{P=1.025(0.20)(89.5)=18.35\ \mathrm{kW}} and
 * @math{Q=0.20(560)=112\ \mathrm{acfm}}.
 *
 * @heading{Assumptions and Limits}
 * - Starting transients, minimum off time, and motor start limits are not modeled.
 * - Validate start/stop applicability with the controller sequence and manufacturer guidance.
 * - Pressure correction follows the selected screw or reciprocating pressure-ratio basis described
 *   in @ref compressor_assessment_pressure_inlet_formula.
 *
 */
